From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:52:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: report denormBehaviorIndependence 32_BIT_ONLY on
 Valhall

PanVK reported VK_SHADER_FLOAT_CONTROLS_INDEPENDENCE_NONE on v9+, which
caps vkd3d-proton's shader model detection at SM 6.0 (SM 6.2+ needs
independent FP16/FP32 denorm modes).

Valhall's FTZ modes cover (FP16, FP32) = (preserve, preserve),
(preserve, flush) "DX11" and (flush, flush) "always". The one pair that
32_BIT_ONLY newly allows and the hardware lacks, flush FP16 + preserve
FP32, now runs in the preserve mode and the compiler flushes FP16 itself
(bi_emulate_ftz_fp16): FLUSH.v2f16.ftz on every FP16 float result
(including FP32->FP16 conversions) and on FP16 float operands that were
not already flushed. Operand flushing is needed because NIR drops an
fcanonicalize whose users are float ops, assuming they flush their
operands as the hardware modes do. Bit-preserving ops are untouched.
FP64 is unsupported, so FP16 and FP64 share a mode trivially.

Only shaders with DenormFlushToZero 16 + DenormPreserve 32 take the new
path; shaders without float controls compile exactly as before.
PANVK_DENORM_INDEP=0 reports NONE again.

With 32_BIT_ONLY, DXVK starts requesting DenormFlushToZero 32 (D3D11
rules), so its shaders run in the DX11 mode, and on v11 floor/ceil
flushed their operand with an extra CVT-pipe FLUSH. Skip that FLUSH
when the operand comes from FADD/FMA (possibly through fneg/fabs/fsat):
the FTZ mode already flushed that result.

Channel: compatibility, unsafe

